"Coursing is team obstacle running; Celena North's Coursing I uses teams of seven."
"No more than five of a team run at once, alternating members."
"Teams submit strategies by Thursday for approval, then run in the gym at 5 AM Friday."
"Two obstacles of each course are announced in advance."
"Captains set five runners and agree to each other's supply lists; odd equipment can be objected to."
"Each runner crossing the finish earns the team one attack; its target may briefly retaliate."
"Teams must tag every obstacle; attacking into a free-combat zone crash restarts the team with penalty."
"Interschool Coursing championships pit Celena North against schools such as Li Jean and Naya Din."
